From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:07:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: decide the EDID and SDR primaries of
 an external sink

A T8132 external connector publishes no EDID, so a compositor sees no
HDR capability on it, and every SDR frame on an external link is
tagged Display P3, which is wrong for an sRGB sink.

Add the pure part of doing better, for the KUnit suite:
- which EDID to publish for the current sink: its own, where its
  DisplayAttributes carry one, else one built from their identity and
  colour (dcp_metadata_edid(), as for the desktop external processors),
  else none; never one received for an earlier sink;
- whether a sink is wide gamut: its CIE 1931 xy primaries span at least
  the mean of the sRGB and the Display P3 triangle areas; without
  usable chromaticity, it takes BT.2020 RGB;
- the primaries of the frames on a link: BT.2020 for PQ or a BT2020_RGB
  Colorspace, Display P3 for a wide gamut sink, else BT.709 (sRGB).

The surface tags are ITU-T H.273 code points (transfer 13 sRGB, 16 PQ;
primaries 9 BT.2020, 12 P3-D65): add BT.709 (1) and let a frame carry
it. Internal panel frames never set it and are tagged as before.

New KUnit suite apple-dcp-m4-ext-sink (6 cases) and one case in
apple-dcp-m4-frame.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
(cherry picked from commit a08e0072559d7e9522f72ed3377433dda4d98184)
(cherry picked from commit 0e9d837f5d70f109b6ff7936a7007d7a8ebabfa4)
